id: pm-xj80p9
title: Keep mutation-event subscriptions available when optional index rebuilds race or contend
description: listMutationEvents treats the optional derived index as mandatory after a successful rebuild and lets rebuild lock contention escape. A concurrent writer or invalidation between rebuild and the next read can throw event_index_unavailable despite valid authoritative JSONL. Bound optional repair attempts and preserve the existing cursor and source contracts through authoritative fallback.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-17T19:35:41.682Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T00:29:52.869Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-18T00:29:51.985Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-18T00:29:51.985Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Isolated public SDK and CLI regressions prove valid history remains readable when index repair is contended or invalidated after rebuild; Optional event-read rebuilds acquire locks without waiting and never retry in a loop; Pagination and subscriptions resume across derived and authoritative pages without lost or duplicate events; Real history corruption remains actionable rather than being swallowed; No public return type or cursor format changes
goal: project management = context management
objective: Keep committed mutation facts available when optional accelerators cannot provide a coherent snapshot
value: Package authors and notification hosts can continue observing valid history without handling avoidable cache outages
why_now: Mixed-reader contention work reproduced both a post-rebuild availability escape and an environment override that defeated fail-fast repair
parent: pm-lvyd
risk: medium
confidence: 95
resolution: Preserve authority-backed event pages when optional repair races or contends; cap built-in lock retries across environment overrides. Show complete background lock options and clarify that confirmed stale ownership may require creation retries while active contention fails fast.
expected_result: "Keep compatible event filters/cursors and authoritative error semantics, with accurate lock-lifecycle guidance for package authors."
actual_result: The linked SDK/lock cohort passes49 tests. All four typecheck projects pass and docs/secret gates pass. Current history coverage diagnostics pass467 tests with every event-index statement/function/branch exercised. Final-head full CI and hosted analysis remain required; optional provider quotas are not approvals.
